Description
[maxangelo987](https://github.com/maxangelo987)
opened [2w ago](https://github.com/MAKASA-LABORATORY/BCIIS-Server/issues/34#issue-5314080742)
Collaborative-only backlog finding
Project: Bohol Cacao System Phase 4Repository / branch: BCIIS-Server/James_Bago @ d7365e90Severity: High
The branch tracks Database Backup/DATABASE_Backup.sql, and the reviewed artifact is not schema-only: it contains populated application records, including business/research-survey content and account/authentication-related rows. No record values, credentials, hashes, or personal details are reproduced in this issue.
Risk
Source control becomes a distribution/history channel for real application/research/PII-like records that do not belong in an implementation repository.
Account/authentication rows and other sensitive operational data increase impact if the repository or its history is exposed beyond the intended audience.
A committed database snapshot can persist in Git history even after a later file deletion.
Required remediation
Stop committing populated database backups/dumps to implementation branches.
Keep only schema definitions, parameterized stored procedures, migrations, and synthetic/non-identifying fixtures needed for development/testing.
Privately assess whether the committed dump contains real production/research/personal/account data; do not paste records into GitHub discussions.
If sensitive/credential-bearing data is confirmed, rotate/revoke affected credentials where applicable and assess Git-history cleanup according to the project’s retention/governance requirements.
Add repository-ignore/pre-commit controls so generated/populated SQL backups are not recommitted.
Add a lightweight CI/review check that rejects populated dump artifacts while allowing approved schema/SP/migration files.
Branch naming
James_Bago is contributor-oriented rather than task/module-oriented. For future implementation work, prefer names such as chore/database-artifact-hygiene, fix/backup-data-governance, or the actual assigned feature/module. This audit does not rename or modify the branch.
Suggested course alignment
DSA W1/W2 — Git/programming review + backend data flow: document the allowed DB artifact boundary and demonstrate schema/SP/migration-only source control with synthetic fixtures and a repository check.
